<header><p class="eyebrow">SOCIAL HISTORY · THE RÍO DE LA PLATA</p><h1>What Was a Pulpería? The Rural Shop at the Heart of Gaucho Life</h1><p class="intro">A pulpería was more than a place to buy provisions. Across the rural Río de la Plata, it could bring neighbors, itinerant workers and travelers together to exchange news, share stories and hear music.</p></header>
<figure class="hero"><img src="/media/cultura-gauchesca/pulperia-gaucha-campana-rioplatense.webp" alt="Modern editorial depiction of a traditional rural pulpería" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Modern editorial illustration. This is not an archival photograph.</figcaption></figure>
